{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-115745",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's compute the step size $Δt,$ which is just the width of each rectangle. In this case, the endpoints of our interval are $a=0$ and $b=75,$ and there are $n=5$ rectangles, so the step size is\n\n$$\nΔt=\\frac{b-a}{n}=\\frac{75-0}{5}=15.\n$$\n\nThe area $A$ under the graph can be approximated using the formula\n\n$$\nA≈(\\overset{\\text{heights}}{\\overset{⏞}{r(15)+r(30)+r(45)+r(60)+r(75)}})\\cdot {{Δt}_{⏟}}_{\\text{width}}.\n$$\n\nSo, we now set up a table with the values of $r(t)$ at each point:\n\n| $t$ | $15$ | $30$ | $45$ | $60$ | $75$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $r(t)$ | $25$ | $35$ | $40$ | $35$ | $25$ |\n\nNow, we obtain the following approximation for the area:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ≈(25+35+40+35+25)\\cdot 15 \\\\  & =160\\cdot 15 \\\\  & =2\\,400\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, in the given context, the area under the curve represents the total number of flour bags made by the machine in $75$ minutes.  So, the number of flour bags is approximately $2\\,400.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-115745\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>First, let's compute the step size <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"58\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c394\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D461 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> which is just the width of each rectangle. In this case, the endpoints of our interval are <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"59\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D44E TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> and <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"60\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D44F TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c37\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c35\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c clas